# Dictionary for `rom_header` and `rom_load`.
#
# Header detection scores candidate offsets, so a purely random image essentially never scores
# above zero — an unseeded campaign spends its whole budget bouncing off `NoValidHeader` and never
# reaches `board::select`, which is the part worth fuzzing. These tokens are the bytes that get a
# mutated input past that gate.

# --- Map modes (`$xxD5`). The value that decides LoROM vs HiROM vs the fast variants. ---
"\x20"
"\x21"
"\x23"
"\x25"
"\x30"
"\x31"
"\x35"

# --- Chipset bytes (`$xxD6`). This is what `board::select` dispatches on, so each value here is a
# different board implementation with its own window arithmetic. ---
"\x00"
"\x02"
"\x03"
"\x13"
"\x14"
"\x15"
"\x1a"
"\x25"
"\x32"
"\x34"
"\x35"
"\x43"
"\x45"
"\xf3"
"\xf5"
"\xf6"
"\xf9"

# --- Zip container magics. `extract_rom_bytes` sniffs these before anything else runs; without
# them the third-party archive path is unreachable. ---
"PK\x03\x04"
"PK\x05\x06"
"PK\x01\x02"
".sfc"
".smc"
".fig"
".swc"
